Ring_a19114.gif\" width=\"32\"/></a></span></span></td>\n<td class=\"pi-horizontal-group-item pi-data-value pi-font pi-border-color pi-item-spacing\" data-source=\"bestloot5\"><span class=\"no-pseudoelements-container\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"#/wiki/Club%20Ring\"><img alt=\"Club Ring\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"32\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Club_Ring_6dc657.gif\" width=\"32\"/></a></span></span></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Maps and Pictures</h2>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"map\">\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><img alt=\"Dwacarta Map\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"170\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Dwacarta_Map_8abcc5.png\" width=\"125\"/></span> </div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Other Properties</h2>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"implemented\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Version</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><span class=\"implementation-date\">6.1<br/>December 23, 2000<br/>Christmas Update 2000</span></div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><p>\t    See also: Hunting Places and Loot <span class=\"explained\">Help</span></p></nav>\n</aside>\n<p><br/>\nAlso known as <b>Kazordoon Prison</b> or <b>Dwacatra Prison Isle</b>. It's name is an reference to the Alcatraz Prison Isle in San Francisco. <b>Dwacatra</b> is the prison island deep below <a href=\"#/wiki/Kazordoon\">Kazordoon</a>. This is where all of the law-breakers are locked away. The general of the dwarven army has the only known <a href=\"#/wiki/Key%203802\">key</a>, and he is not likely to let just anyone have it. He keeps it safely locked away in his chambers.\n</p><p><a href=\"#/wiki/Sorcerer\">Sorcerers</a> and <a href=\"#/wiki/Druid\">Druids</a> of <a href=\"#/wiki/Level\">Level</a> 27 and above can hunt here with little waste with 2 <a href=\"#/wiki/Monk%20%28Creature%29\">Monks</a> as summons, other summons don't work so well because they can't heal themselves. Don't care about <a href=\"#/wiki/Food\">Food</a>, because <a href=\"#/wiki/Cyclops\">Cyclopses</a> and <a href=\"#/wiki/Dwarves\">Dwarves</a> drop enough <a href=\"#/wiki/Meat\">Meat</a> and <a href=\"#/wiki/White%20Mushroom\">White Mushroom</a>. Some Stalagmite Runes would be good too, to deal with <a href=\"#/wiki/Orc%20Berserker\">Orc Berserkers</a>.\n</p><p><b>Dwacatra</b> has some small holes and open holes with <a href=\"#/wiki/Creatures\">Creatures</a>. Don't go there without <a href=\"#/wiki/Rope\">Ropes</a> nor <a href=\"#/wiki/Shovel\">Shovels</a>. <a href=\"#/wiki/Obsidian%20Knife\">Obsidian Knife</a> will help you a lot, because there's lots of <a href=\"#/wiki/Minotaurs\">Minotaurs</a>.\n</p><p><b>Statistics:</b><br/>\nAverage of Experience obtained:\n</p>\n<ul><li>10-20k/hour.</li></ul>\n<p>Average of Money obtained:\n</p>\n<ul><li>500-1000<a href=\"#/wiki/Gold%20Coin\">gps</a>/hour.</li></ul>\n<p>Dropped Items:<br/>\n<i><b>See the principal article: Loot/Dwacatra</b></i>\n</p>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div><table cellspacing=\"0\" class=\"wikitable sortable full-width\"><caption>Surface of Dwacatra</caption><tbody><tr><th>Name</th><th data-sort-type=\"number\" style=\"width: 38px; text-align: center;\">Exp</th><th data-sort-type=\"number\" style=\"text-align: center;\">HP</th><th data-sort-type=\"number\" style=\"text-align: center;\">Max. Damage</th><th style=\"font-size: small;\">Loot</th></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"width: 100px; text-align: center\"><span class=\"no-pseudoelements-cont